cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Agent-Judge-Framework: A Reliability-Oriented Framework for Automated Evaluation of Tool-Using Autonomous Agents"
message: "If you use this research, data, or code, please cite as below."
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
license: MIT
abstract: |
  A reliability-oriented framework designed to evaluate tool-using
  autonomous agents while simultaneously assessing the reliability of
  the evaluation process itself.

  The proposed architecture consists of four interconnected layers:
  Knowledge and Evidence, Agent Execution, Independent Evaluation, and
  Judge Reliability Assessment. The experimental design compares three
  agent configurations, two independent LLM judges, and two evaluation
  strategies: zero-shot evaluation and structured evidence-based
  evaluation.

  The framework will produce an executable Python implementation, a
  reproducible benchmark, an evaluation dataset, and an empirical
  research report. No experimental results are claimed in this
  manuscript. All hypotheses remain subject to empirical investigation.
keywords:
  - autonomous agents
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - evaluation reliability
  - tool execution
  - evidence verification
  - judge calibration
  - benchmark design
